VECTOR NETWORK — COMPLETE REPOSITORY REPAIR, IMPLEMENTATION AND ACCEPTANCE MANDATE

MISSION

You are responsible for bringing Vector Network to a genuinely operational, secure, internally consistent and independently verifiable decentralized network.

This is an implementation mandate, not a request for recommendations, another audit report, a design proposal or a list of future improvements.

Your job is to find and fix everything that is incomplete, incorrect, insecure, inconsistent, broken, misleading or not working across the Vector Network repositories.

Do not stop after fixing the defects listed in this prompt. Perform a complete engineering audit, discover additional defects independently, and fix those as well.

Do not simply make the tests pass by weakening validation, disabling functionality, skipping tests, introducing mocks into production paths or changing the specifications to accommodate broken implementations.

The final result must be working software whose behavior is demonstrated by executable tests and real distributed processes.

1. REPOSITORIES

Work across all three repositories:

1. Kernel: https://github.com/vnetworkx/v-kernelx
2. Vector Language: https://github.com/vnetworkx/vectorspace
3. Documentation: https://github.com/vnetworkx/docs

Inspect the latest actual contents and commit history of all repositories before making changes.

