14. Do not introduce undocumented protocol assumptions, invented economic values or arbitrary security exceptions.
15. Preserve valid existing functionality and user work.
16. Do not force-push, rewrite history, reset away user changes or discard unrelated work.
17. Do not deploy to production, move real assets or modify production infrastructure.
18. Do not expose private keys, secrets, credentials or populated environment files in source control, logs or reports.

Do not stop when the first test passes. Continue through the entire acceptance process.

When a test exposes another defect, fix it and rerun the relevant tests. When one fix breaks another component, fix the integration rather than leaving an inconsistent repository.

If the execution environment genuinely prevents a task from being completed, identify the precise blocker and complete every other possible task. Never report an unexecuted test as passing.

